# Docs link direction

Insights are commentary. G.A.I.N, blueprints, and playbooks are the durable product docs. Architecture companions are unlisted detail pages for System Design insights. Links go **from insights into product docs**, never the reverse, except the architecture ↔ parent pair below.

| Source | May link to `/insights/…` | May link to `/architecture/…` | May link to G.A.I.N / blueprints / playbooks |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Insights** (`docs/insights/`) | Yes (other published insights) | Yes (that insight's companion only) | Yes |
| **Architecture** (`docs/architecture/`) | **Parent insight only** | No | Yes |
| **G.A.I.N** (`docs/frameworks/`) | **No** | **No** | Yes |
| **Blueprints** (`docs/blueprints/`) | **No** | **No** | Yes |
| **Playbooks** (`docs/playbooks/`) | **No** | **No** | Yes |

Draft targets are a separate ban: `.cursor/rules/no-links-to-draft-articles.mdc`.

## Do

```markdown
# Insight → product docs (allowed)
Full reference: [Agents Blueprint](/blueprints/agents-blueprint).
How-to: [Autonomy shape](/playbooks/agents/orchestration/autonomy-shape).
Principles: [G.A.I.N Agents](/frameworks/gain-agents).
```

## Do not

```markdown
# G.A.I.N / blueprint / playbook → insight (forbidden)
Decision guide: [Enterprise AI Workflow Patterns](/insights/enterprise-ai-workflow-patterns-autonomy-vs-control)
```

Keep the same idea as plain text, or link a product-doc page instead.

Architecture companions may include **Parent insight:** `[{title}](/insights/{parent-slug})`. That is the only `/insights/` href allowed from `docs/architecture/`.

## Before finishing

1. New or edited `docs/frameworks/**`, `docs/blueprints/**`, `docs/playbooks/**`: no `/insights/` or `/architecture/` hrefs.
2. New or edited insights: outbound `/frameworks/`, `/blueprints/`, `/playbooks/`, and that story's `/architecture/…` companion is fine.
3. New or edited `docs/architecture/**` (except `index.mdx`): `/insights/` only for the parent System Design insight.
4. Do not add inbound links to an insight from G.A.I.N, blueprints, or playbooks (including `remove-draft` suggestions).
